Choose tags for this document in paperless-ngx, only from the list of available tags below.

Tags say what area of life a document belongs to (money, health, work, the car, the home...), plus a few kinds of paper the owner wants to find together (reports, certificates). Who sent it is kept elsewhere, so tags never name the sender.

Rules:
- Choose 1 to 4 tags, the ones that clearly fit. One is fine. Never more than 4, plus "translation" when it applies.
- "translation": the document is a translation of another document (it says "translation", "certified translation", "ترجمة", "tercüme", "çeviri", "Übersetzung", or carries a translator's stamp or statement), or holds an original together with its translation. Never for a paper that is simply written in two languages side by side.
- Use only tags exactly as written in the list. Never invent a tag, never change a tag's spelling.
- Never choose any of these, even if they are in the list: ai-new, locked, unlocked, and any tag starting with "paperless-gpt". They are used by the system, not for topics.
- "medical": anything from doctors, clinics, hospitals, labs or pharmacies about care or medicine: lab tests, prescriptions, x-ray and scan reports, doctors' notes, sick leave, vaccination records, medicines bought. Always together with "health". "health" and "medical" are only for care and medicine: never for food, groceries or a supermarket receipt.
- "laboratory": the result of a lab test: blood tests (CBC, vitamins, cholesterol...), urine tests, pathology, cultures. Always together with "health" and "medical", whether or not the page says "laboratory".
- "report": a paper that reports findings: medical, lab, x-ray and scan reports, inspection or assessment reports. Never an invoice, a letter or a certificate.
- "certificate": any certificate: salary, experience, education, training, completion, birth, marriage.
- "employment": about a job itself: employment contracts, offer letters, work visas, labour cards and work permits, salary and experience certificates, resignation and end of service papers. Usually together with "work".
- "government" only for papers issued by a government body (ministries, police, immigration, municipality, courts), never for a company's paper.
- "important" only for papers that are hard to replace: IDs, passports, visas, contracts, deeds, certificates of education. Never for medical papers, tickets, bookings, receipts, bills, resumes or CVs, or letters.
- "salary": always on a salary certificate, a payslip or a salary transfer letter, together with "work".
- "shopping" only for buying goods: a shop, pharmacy or online-order receipt or invoice. Never for hotel or travel bookings, tickets, bills, fines or services.
- "tax" only when the paper is about tax itself (a tax return, a tax certificate). VAT printed on a receipt does not make it a tax paper.
- When unsure about a tag, leave it out.

Examples (made up; choose from the real list below, not from here):
- A salary certificate from an employer: work, employment, salary, certificate
- A blood test result: health, medical, laboratory, report
- A doctor's prescription: health, medical
- An x-ray report: health, medical, report
- A pharmacy receipt for medicine: health, medical, shopping
- A supermarket receipt for food: shopping
- An employment contract: work, employment, important
- A traffic fine from the police: car, government
- A tenancy contract: home, rent, important
- A flight ticket: travel
- A phone bill: utilities

Reply with the chosen tags only, comma separated, on one line, with no other words.

<available_tags>
{{.AvailableTags | join ", "}}
</available_tags>

<title>
{{.Title}}
</title>

<content>
{{.Content}}
</content>
